From: momokind <momokind2002@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] RK3588: default Dolby Vision Chroma MMR arithmetic to Float

On RK3588 (Mali-G610 MC4 with Mesa PanVK), heavy Profile 7 FEL discs whose
RPU triggers SPLIT_GUARD / mmr_exact64() or mmr_wide() (128-bit emulated MMR)
exceed the 4K24 frame budget and exhibit momentary green flashes and audio
stuttering. Defaulting Chroma MMR to Float avoids the 64/128-bit emulated
shader paths while keeping Exact / Split / Exact (64-bit) selectable in
Expert settings.

--- a/system/settings/settings.xml
+++ b/system/settings/settings.xml
@@ -375,7 +375,7 @@
             <dependency type="enable" setting="videoplayer.allowedhdrformats" operator="contains">0</dependency>
           </dependencies>
           <level>3</level>
-          <default>0</default>
+          <default>3</default>
           <constraints>
             <options>
               <option label="36649">0</option>
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/HwDecRender/DVTunnelDRMPRIME.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/HwDecRender/DVTunnelDRMPRIME.h
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@
       bool operator==(const Metadata& other) const = default;
     };
 
-    pi_mmr_mode mmr = PI_MMR_EXACT;
+    pi_mmr_mode mmr = PI_MMR_FLOAT;
     pi_filters filters = PI_FILTERS_CB1;
     pi_el_upscale elUpscale = PI_EL_BILINEAR;
     //! render the enhancement layer where the RPU needs it (FEL); false: the base layer alone
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoSettings.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoSettings.cpp
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@
   m_DolbyVision = true;
   m_DolbyVisionEL = VS_DOLBYVISION_EL_AUTO;
   m_DolbyVisionUpscale = VS_DOLBYVISION_UPSCALE_BILINEAR;
-  m_DolbyVisionMMR = VS_DOLBYVISION_MMR_EXACT;
+  m_DolbyVisionMMR = VS_DOLBYVISION_MMR_FLOAT;
   m_DolbyVisionFilters = VS_DOLBYVISION_FILTERS_CB1;
   m_DolbyVisionInfoframe = VS_DOLBYVISION_INFOFRAME_AUTO;
   m_DolbyVisionCM4 = VS_DOLBYVISION_CM4_OFF;
